  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> be the respective sum of the first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms, the next <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms and the next <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms of a geometric progression, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> are in"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "arithmetic progression",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "geometric progression",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "harmonic progression",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> be the 1<sup>st </sup>term and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> be the common ratio of the given G.P.<br /><br />Sum of the first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms of the G.P. is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. The next <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms form a G.P. series of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms with the first term as the <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> term of the given G.P. is given by <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math> . Sum of the next <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> terms of the G.P. is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>⇒&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> <math><mo>⇒&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> are in G.P."
  }
}